Add a built-in "simple" frame-difference motion detector

The vendor IVS algorithms in this T23 libimp are unusable:

  - algorithm = move       IMP_IVS_CreateChn succeeds, then rvd takes a
                           SIGSEGV (epc=0, ra=0 — a call through a NULL
                           function pointer) as soon as frames flow.
  - algorithm = base_move  IMP_IVS_CreateBaseMoveInterface returns a handle
                           but IMP_IVS_CreateChn rejects it with -1.

Both fail inside the blob with the HAL calling correctly, so there is nothing
to work around at our level.

This adds algorithm = simple, which skips the IVS pipeline entirely and reads
NV12 frames straight from FrameSource — the same route the JZDL standalone
path already uses, and an API the encoder exercises every frame, so it is
known good on this SoC. Each grid zone's mean luma is compared against the
previous processed frame; a zone is active when the mean shifts by more than
the sensitivity threshold.

Only the Y plane is touched, subsampled 4x in both axes (~3.6k byte loads per
frame for a 640x360 sub-stream at the default 4x4 grid), and results are fed
to the existing ivs_process_move_result() so OSD, RMD and recording see the
same state the vendor "move" algorithm produced.

Costs no extra libraries: IVS_DETECT stays off, so libjzdl and libstdc++
(~655 KB compressed) are not linked.

